@startuml
title C1 UML -> model2owl -> SHACL -> schema-automator -> LinkML (round trip)
participant "EA UML (XMI)" as UML
participant "model2owl (XSLT)" as M2O
participant "schemauto import-shacl" as SA
participant "Curated LinkML overlay" as LML
participant "gen-shacl" as GS
participant "Equivalence check (CI)" as EQ
UML -> M2O : XMI export (SEMIC conventions)
M2O -> M2O : conventions report (SVRL) gate
M2O -> SA : OWL + SHACL shapes (sh:targetClass, sh:class, sh:datatype, sh:in, sh:sparql)
SA -> SA : drop sh:sparql, sh:minInclusive, sh:pattern, paths; rdf:langString -> string
SA -> LML : classes with class_uri, slots with slot_uri (identifier only if --identifier)
LML -> LML : add identifier, aggregate annotations, lang-string convention, enum meaning
LML -> GS : regenerate shapes
GS -> EQ : LinkML SHACL (sh:closed true by default)
M2O -> EQ : model2owl SHACL
EQ --> LML : report drift (dropped constraints listed)
note over SA, LML : Lossy by construction (shacl_import_engine.py:35-110); validation stays on model2owl SHACL
@enduml
